	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvista uses the camera to record your drive and to detect vehicles, people, bikes, traffic lights and stop signs. Video is analysed on this iPhone and kept in local storage; it is never uploaded.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvista uses your location while the app is open to show your position on the map, calculate routes, show speed and local weather, and tag saved incident clips. During active turn-by-turn navigation it keeps using your location when you leave the app or lock the screen, so spoken directions continue; it is never used in the background otherwise.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvista uses the microphone only if you turn on audio for recorded clips, and to listen for your spoken cancel phrase during an emergency countdown. Speech is recognised on this iPhone when supported; audio is not uploaded by Corvista.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvista saves incident clips you choose to export to your photo library. It cannot read your existing photos.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvista recognises your spoken cancel phrase (for example "cancel") during an emergency countdown. Recognition runs on this iPhone when your language supports it; otherwise Apple processes the audio to recognise it.</string>
